1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, fame, power.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,817
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,020
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:52,597
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:58,417
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,837
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:06,737
Is only legendary?

20
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:10,117
Till someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,557
Through it all.

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,477
Through all the trouble and times.

23
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,320
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,220
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:30,520
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

27
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,020
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

28
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:42,480
There's always room for you
if you want to be my friend.

29
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,880
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

31
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,117
Ah! My hat! Where's my hat?

32
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,580
It's right there. Calm
down. Oh, good. Here it is.

33
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,621
Have a good nap?

34
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:14,200
Hey, those pirates!

35
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,340
They're gone now, all thanks to you. Me?

36
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:22,351
Yeah, and Ginny asked me to tell you
that he said, see you on the Grand Line.

37
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,840
Huh. He did? To you?

38
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,400
No, to you!

39
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,250
So,

40
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:32,957
I guess I don't have to do any more lame-o

41
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:35,297
chores since I got those
pirates off your back,

42
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,210
right?

43
00:02:36,293 --> 00:02:37,123
That's the deal.

44
00:02:37,206 --> 00:02:38,497
Hey, I was wondering...

45
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:41,815
No, I'm not gonna run away
with you to become a pirate.

46
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,417
I've got some unfinished business here.

47
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,971
I'll stay until Zef acknowledges my skill.

48
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:49,820
Okay, then. I give up.

49
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:52,160
That means you let go!

50
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:57,600
I can't just leave.

51
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:01,577
These bozos don't know the first
thing about how to run a restaurant.

52
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:06,460
But still, I promised myself that one of
these days, I'll go to the Grand Line.

53
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:10,771
Well, let's go right now!

54
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:13,215
It just isn't the right time, not yet.

55
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,760
There is one place.

56
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:20,292
Say, have you ever heard of the all-blue?

57
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:24,740
Nuh-uh You've got to be kidding
me That sea is a miracle

58
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:30,397
In the all-blue there are fish
from the east-blue, the west-blue,

59
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:34,656
the north-blue, and the south-blue
That one stretch of ocean has it all

60
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,300
To us cooks,

61
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,137
it's a culinary dream
come true A place that

62
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,117
fantastic has got to be on
the Grand Line somewhere,

63
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,030
right?

64
00:03:44,113 --> 00:03:44,943
I mean, where else?

65
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:50,000
The little Bratman's truly happy.

66
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:52,960
What an idiot.

67
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,680
All right, guys, soup's on!

68
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,390
Really?

69
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:13,740
Oh, good.

70
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:16,157
They saved us some seats. They did?

71
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,040
No chairs left for you.

72
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:20,960
Just sit on the floor and eat.

73
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,400
There are no chairs?

74
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,052
That doesn't seem right.

75
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:25,920
This is a restaurant.

76
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,960
All right, fine.

77
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,946
They sure are acting strange.

78
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,020
Well, that's nothing new.

79
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,100
Bunch of jerks.

80
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,020
Hey, what is this?

81
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:40,057
Who prepared the soup this morning?

82
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:41,380
Oh, I did.

83
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,137
The stuff is pretty good, huh?

84
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:46,000
I think I really outdid
myself. Is that a joke?

85
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:48,380
I can barely hold this slop down!

86
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,400
I thought someone like
you would like slop.

87
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:02,120
It makes sense to me, seeing
as that's what pigs like. Ha!

88
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:05,780
Just face it, Sanji, your
soup sucks! It's disgusting!

89
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:11,000
That soup is nothing short of a delicacy.

90
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,867
There's something wrong
with your taste buds.

91
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:20,200
Blah, that's gross!

92
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:23,400
I can't eat this!

93
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:26,970
Revolting!

94
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:28,620
This soup is horrible!

95
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:38,840
What the hell's going on, you bastards?

96
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,877
We're sick of the way you run things.

97
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:43,657
You're a sham of a sous-chef
and everybody knows it.

98
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:47,197
You can't just settle every single
little disagreement with violence.

99
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,809
If the food's bad, then
we're gonna say so.

100
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:51,820
What'd you say?

101
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,430
Boss!

102
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:58,670
He's her.

103
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:04,260
That wretched little dish
tasted like stewed garbage.

104
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:08,521
If we ever served that kind of
trash here, we'd go out of business.

105
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,837
Are you really this stupid?

106
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:14,660
Just how is my soup any different
from the stuff you make? How?

107
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:16,528
You think they're the same?

108
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,940
Don't flatter yourself.

109
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:25,280
The boss punched him.

110
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:26,600
He didn't kick him.

111
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:30,277
You think you can lecture me
on the art of cooking, do you?

112
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,220
Fat chance.

113
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:35,696
I'm a man who has cooked on more seas
than days that you've been alive.

114
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:40,850
Damn it!

115
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,390
Gah!

116
00:06:51,473 --> 00:06:52,857
What's all the fuss about?

117
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:54,587
This soup's totally awesome!

118
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,780
All of us know the soup is good.

119
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:59,480
I know he's an outstanding chef.

120
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:01,820
Everyone here on the Baratier does.

121
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,440
Yeah, he's great.

122
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:06,311
Aside from Chef Zef, he's the best we got.

123
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:08,040
That was scary, wasn't it?

124
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:10,120
He seriously snapped. Yeah.

125
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:21,264
But that thick-skulled idiot wouldn't
listen to us if we tried to reason with him.

126
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,080
Hey, listen.

127
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,417
You were saying that you needed
a cook for your ship, right?

128
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:32,357
Well, this isn't something
I want to be asking anyone,

129
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:36,280
but would you mind taking that
little brat along with you?

130
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,640
Take him to the Grand Line.

131
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,540
That would be best for him.

132
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:44,020
The Grand Line is his dream.

133
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:49,517
Jeez, boss, you sure made
us put on a hell of a show!

134
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:52,297
Oh, man, I was worried you
was gonna figure it out.

135
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:53,968
Because of your bad acting.

136
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:57,577
Come on, your acting
was way worse than mine.

137
00:07:57,660 --> 00:07:59,277
I'm gonna get some more
of that scene, too.

138
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,900
Yeah, that stuff is good.

139
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:18,740
I can hear everything, you dumbasses.

140
00:08:21,060 --> 00:08:22,660
So what do you say, kid?

141
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:24,490
No way!

142
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:29,872
But earlier you mentioned you
needed a cook for your ship.

143
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:32,742
Just what are you trying to say?

144
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:35,197
That he's suddenly not
good enough for you?

145
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,337
Oh, he's good.

146
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:39,596
And I'd love it if he joined
my crew and came with us.

147
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:44,277
But it seems like he really wants to
stay here and cook with all of you guys.

148
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:47,897
You can ask me all you want, but
I'm just not going to take him.

149
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:52,745
So you're saying you can't agree to it
until he tells you himself, is that right?

150
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:53,910
That's right.

151
00:08:53,993 --> 00:08:54,823
More food, please.

152
00:08:54,906 --> 00:08:56,939
Well, I suppose that's fair enough.

153
00:08:57,660 --> 00:09:01,917
But who knows if that hard-headed little
brat will ever agree to join up with him.

154
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:07,140
Yeah, once that guy makes up his mind,
there's nothing anybody can do to change it.

155
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,250
More, please!

156
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:39,360
Sanji, what is that?

157
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,500
A fish man?

158
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:43,057
Did he come all the way from
Fishman Islands to eat here?

159
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:43,970
You dolt!

160
00:09:44,053 --> 00:09:45,546
It's a human and a pan shark!

161
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,170
Who's this?

162
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:48,620
Whoa, it's Yosaku!

163
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,220
Oh, hey, big bro Luffy.

164
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:52,877
How come you're alone?

165
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,790
Where are the others?

166
00:09:53,873 --> 00:09:54,919
Did you find Nami?

167
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:06,257
We never actually caught up to her, but
from the direction Big Sis is headed,

168
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:09,317
we think we've figured out where
she's going and what she plans to do.

169
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,230
I see.

170
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:11,968
Then we can bring her back.

171
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:13,930
Maybe.

172
00:10:14,013 --> 00:10:16,877
It's just, if our suspicions
turn out to be true,

173
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,737
then the place she
intends to go could mean

174
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:21,467
certain death for all
of us if we follow her.

175
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:25,596
The point is, we really need
your help, Big Bro Luffy.

176
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:27,120
Please, come with me!

177
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:30,820
Okay, I don't really get
it, but I got it. Let's go.

178
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,190
Wait.

179
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,040
Your dream is foolish.

180
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,840
Then again, so's mine.

181
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,360
Now is as good a time as any.

182
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:52,561
Why not start my quest right now?

183
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,750
Sanji?

184
00:10:56,040 --> 00:11:00,452
I'll be joining your little crew on
your journey to be king of the pirates.

185
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,640
You hear me?

186
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:07,940
I want to be the cook on your
ship. All right. What do you say?

187
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,980
Yeah, of course!

188
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:14,080
This is great, Big Bro Luffy! Woo-hoo!

189
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,460
We gotta cook!

190
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,097
Now we'll get the tasty food!

191
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:18,010
We gotta cook!

192
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:20,124
Are you guys happy now or what?

193
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:21,930
Sorry.

194
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,480
Really, I'll leave now.

195
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,660
I don't like it.

196
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:26,817
To tell you the truth,

197
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:29,517
I was hoping to give you the boot
from this restaurant personally.

198
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:33,817
But it seems that you don't have a
problem with straight-up abandoning us

199
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:38,880
I'm especially sorry for making the lot
of you resort to bad acting. Hey, wait.

200
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,002
How'd you know?

201
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:43,160
I heard everything you
bunch of jerks. What?

202
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:47,177
Was stomping on my pride the best
plan that you could come up with

203
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:52,300
was it you damn geezer Every little
thing has to be a fight with you.

204
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,760
I'm sick and tired of it. Bring it on

205
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:56,610
Hmm.

206
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:58,348
I have never liked children

207
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,376
As a matter of fact, I hate children.

208
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,937
There wasn't a day past
when I didn't regret

209
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:06,317
letting a useless little
brat like you live,

210
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:07,230
Sanji.

211
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,210
Ha!

212
00:12:08,293 --> 00:12:09,840
Fine by me, you rotten old man.

213
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,595
Enjoy the rest of your miserable life.

214
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:14,210
Whoa!

215
00:12:14,293 --> 00:12:15,316
This is a nice ship!

216
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,737
You sure it's okay to use her?

217
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:17,650
Of course.

218
00:12:17,733 --> 00:12:18,758
It's Sanjay's ship.

219
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:22,020
You still need more? Yep.

220
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,457
Gonna need more meat.

221
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:24,370
All right.

222
00:12:24,453 --> 00:12:26,417
Well, how many days are
you gonna be out at sea?

223
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:27,330
I don't know.

224
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:34,980
It's the nicest sea restaurant
I've ever seen, that's for sure.

225
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,700
Hey, Sanji, listen Huh?

226
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:01,837
What is it?

227
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:05,740
It doesn't matter what sort of
person walks through our doors.

228
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:09,080
If they're hungry, then they will be fed.

229
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:13,451
Every starving wretch who comes
to us will get a fine meal.

230
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,117
We can make that happen.

231
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,318
It doesn't matter how much we fight.

232
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,680
Because we share the same dream. Ha! Yeah!

233
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:23,760
Are you ready?

234
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,457
Because we're going to be busy.

235
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:26,370
You bet!

236
00:13:26,453 --> 00:13:28,536
It won't be a problem with me around.

237
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:42,610
Awful.

238
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,540
Is that what you call peeling?

239
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,960
That hurt you, old fart.

240
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:50,632
I'm trying to cook here.

241
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,457
Just stay out of my way and
we won't have any problems.

242
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:54,620
Got it? What?

243
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:57,017
You better watch your
mouth, you little brat.

244
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:59,780
I'm not a little brat,
you crusty old geezer.

245
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:05,040
Ha! Try this!

246
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:07,380
Did you make it all by yourself?

247
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:08,850
Uh-huh!

248
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:11,840
How is it?

249
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:15,440
This is the worst soup I've
ever had, you little brat!

250
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,840
You mean old geezer!

251
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:31,160
Big Bro Cook sure is
taking his time. Yeah.

252
00:14:41,680 --> 00:14:43,440
Now it's payback time!

253
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:45,040
Here it comes, Sanji!

254
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:53,740
Really, guys, that was just dumb.

255
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:08,700
Let's get going.

256
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:10,745
You don't need to say goodbye?

257
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:12,640
No, it's fine.

258
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:16,560
Sanji, take care of yourself, okay?

259
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,920
Chef Sam!

260
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,340
Thanks, you geezer.

261
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:39,502
I'll never forget your kindness.

262
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:42,480
I owe my life to you, old man.

263
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,260
So thank you!

264
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:05,420
You asshole!

265
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:11,260
I'm gonna miss you so much!

266
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,480
I'll miss you too!

267
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:40,420
Damn wusses.

268
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:43,917
Real men should part without a word!

269
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,140
Let alone tears.

270
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:49,540
Let's go!

271
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,037
Set sail.

272
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:53,017
I will see you again.

273
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:54,720
I'll come back someday.

274
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:57,010
Bye.

275
00:16:57,093 --> 00:16:59,260
Bye. Bye. Bye. Bye.

276
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:12,600
As long as you sail with enough faith
in yourself, that you have no fear,

277
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,180
not even of death,?

278
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:17,080
you will find the all-blue.

279
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,140
I'm sure of you.

280
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:22,780
All right, men.

281
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,887
Customers will be here soon.

282
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:26,600
Get to work already.

283
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:36,357
As a kid, I never stopped.

284
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,917
Searching for a great treasure.

285
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:43,697
I had a map in my mind.

286
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:46,357
That I knew would lead me.

287
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:50,537
I had to find my way to that place.

288
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:53,437
Before someone could beat me.

289
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:57,617
The promised land was in my grasp.

290
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,980
And I wouldn't let go.

291
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:06,760
La, la,

292
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:13,560
la, la, la, I won't stop
chasing it until it comes true.

293
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:21,957
But if the world ever
changes, I call out your name.

294
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:28,497
We could return to the time
when everything's the same.

295
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:32,900
As long as I'm with you,

296
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:35,897
my memories won't fade.

297
00:18:35,980 --> 00:18:40,960
Waiting for that one true dream?
